FINDINGS:
1. [MAJOR] src/repl/mod.rs:1920 — time_runs executes in the session VM but never calls record_definitions (src/repl/mod.rs:1054), so a binding made by measurement has no Definition — why it matters: lookup finds it but origin_of has no span, so .which reports unknown for a name :inspect finds, the same stale-span class the reset fix removed — concrete fix: call record_definitions for the measured source on success, or document that measured bindings are invisible to .which.
2. [MAJOR] src/repl/mod.rs:1932 — time_runs loops vm.run_quietly N times with no fork and no ask_questions guard, unlike evaluate_for_question at src/repl/mod.rs:1721 — why it matters: every EFFECTFUL_BUILTINS name (src/stdlib.rs:1216: files_write, files_delete, network_get/post, time_sleep, random_*) executes 10-10000 times, repeating destructive/filesystem/network/clock effects and advancing RANDOM_STATE — concrete fix: refuse effectful calls by name like .type does, or limit effectful measurements to 1 run.
3. [MAJOR] src/repl/mod.rs:1937 — only the say buffer is drained via take_output; print and console.log bypass it (src/interpreter.rs:1351), so .bench print "x" writes N lines to the terminal, up to MAX_RUNS 10000 — why it matters: unbounded terminal output with no cap, admitted in FINDINGS.md but still shippable — concrete fix: run measurements with asking_a_question set so print is suppressed, or refuse print/console statements in split_runs/time_runs.
4. [MAJOR] tests/repl_color_test.rs:212 — COLUMNS_LOCK at tests/repl_color_test.rs:22 is taken only by tests at :290 and :313, but a_coloured_banner_paints_both_halves at :212 does two banner_text calls with no lock and asserts strip-equality, and the_banner_is_ascii at :254 writes REDBLUE_ASCII while every banner_text reads it at src/repl/banner.rs:85 — why it matters: the race the lock claims to fix remains for any reader-vs-writer pair, so the suite can still flake — concrete fix: take the same lock in every test that calls banner_text or mutates COLUMNS/REDBLUE_ASCII, or pass width as an argument per FINDINGS.md.
5. [MINOR] src/repl/mod.rs:1920 — time_runs never calls arm_debugger (src/repl/mod.rs:1141) unlike run_program at src/repl/mod.rs:1181 — why it matters: breakpoints/steps armed at the prompt are ignored during measurement, or a stale hook with a previous source runs against measured lines — concrete fix: arm the debugger for the measured source or explicitly clear/set the hook around the timing loop.
